{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Besides the burnt offering of the ox</b> Scripture needed to mention this here to teach that the people's burnt offering does not exempt the daily burnt offering (עֹלַת הַתָּמִיד) and does not precede it. There was no need to mention this during the days of ordination (יְמֵי הַמִּלּוּאִים), because those are individual offerings to fill the hand of the priests, and it is well known that they did not exempt the daily offering nor precede it. In Torat Kohanim (Shemini Milu'im 12) they taught: \"And he burned it upon the altar besides the burnt offering of the morning\" — what does this come to teach us? If to teach that if he found no meal offering he should bring an animal — but has it not already been said (Leviticus 9:16), \"And he brought the burnt offering and offered it according to the ordinance\"? If so, why is it said, \"And he burned it upon the altar besides the burnt offering of the morning\"? It teaches that there were two meal offerings there, one for the burnt offering and one on its own. And its explanation is that if it had said, \"And he brought the burnt offering and offered it according to the ordinance besides the burnt offering of the morning,\" it would have taught that the daily offering comes first, as it says in the portion of the additional offerings, \"Upon the daily burnt offering it shall be prepared, with its libation\" (Numbers 28:15), \"Besides the daily burnt offering\" (ibid. verse 31). But when it mentions the meal offering — \"And he brought the meal offering and filled his hand from it and burned it upon the altar besides the burnt offering of the morning\" — it appears to be referring to the meal offering. Therefore they scrutinized precisely: if you say that he offered this meal offering alone, and did not offer a meal offering of libations for the daily offering nor for the people's burnt offering, such that he found nothing but this freewill offering — but has it not already been said, \"And he brought the burnt offering and offered it according to the ordinance,\" meaning it was offered according to its ordinance with a meal offering of libations? If so, why is it said, \"And he brought and burned it upon the altar besides the burnt offering of the morning\"? To say that he offered this meal offering besides the burnt offering of the morning and its meal offering, for this meal offering is not a meal offering of libations but rather a freewill meal offering of Israel."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The citation 'שמיני מלואים יב' refers to a section in Torat Kohanim (Sifra); the exact numeration follows the Hebrew as written. The word מנחת נסכים literally means 'meal offering of libations' — i.e., the grain component accompanying drink offerings."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:52:08.801840504Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}